# models.manifest — the model weights a deployment must have on disk.
#
# Weights are NOT in git and there is no artifact store: a person copies them to
# the server. This file says which ones, which version, and how to tell that the
# right bytes are in place.
#
# One model per line, whitespace-separated, six columns:
#
#   name   location   subdir   version   checksum   restart
#
#   name      short name; also names the file list models/<name>.files
#   location  a config/deploy.env variable holding a directory (e.g. VS_CT_MODELS_DIR),
#             or an absolute path
#   subdir    the model's directory under location
#   version   a label for people (date, training run, paper version)
#   checksum  sha256 of models/<name>.files, or UNMEASURED
#   restart   comma-separated systemd units to restart when the model changes, or "-"
#
# What the checksum covers. models/<name>.files lists EVERY file in the model
# directory with its size, and a sha256 for the files that decide the model's
# behaviour: weights and configuration (*.pth *.pt *.ckpt *.onnx *.json *.pkl
# *.yaml *.yml). Other files (logs, validation outputs, images) are listed by size
# only. The checksum column is the sha256 of that list, so one short value pins all
# sizes and all weight hashes.
#
# Two ways to check a model against its list:
#   quick  every listed file is present with the listed size       scripts/verify-models.sh
#          (no file is read; fast enough for scripts/health.sh)
#   full   quick, plus re-hash every file that has a sha256         scripts/verify-models.sh --full
#          (reads the weights; minutes for multi-GB models; run by upgrade.sh
#          before it records a model, and on demand)
# Quick does not notice a weight file overwritten by another of exactly the same
# size. Full does.
#
# To measure a model on the server:   scripts/model-manifest.sh --name <name> --write
# A change of version or checksum here is an upgrade: scripts/upgrade.sh names the
# model, tells you to put it in place by hand, verifies it in full, restarts the
# units in the restart column and records it in $VS_STATE_DIR/deployed.models.
#
# The three models below were measured on Ludwig on 2026-11-11 from
# /home/jileihao/data/spt/{ct,tee}-model/models (files dated 2026-07-19). They have
# no upstream version label, so the version column records the capture date.
# A model listed as UNMEASURED has no file list yet: only its directory is checked.

ct-loocv-f0  VS_CT_MODELS_DIR  Dataset900_LOOCV_f0  captured-2026-11-11  5965f5a5028c1af8147fb40ecfd04e25664d22519c8b6133bb0967e6b2bdf5ef  valvescope-handler
